Mindmesh migrations (Alembic)
=============================

The URL comes from DATABASE_URL (app.config), not alembic.ini. Run from backend/:

    alembic upgrade head                         # apply migrations
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add x"   # after editing a models*.py file; review the diff!
    alembic downgrade -1

Switching from create_all (today's boot behaviour in app/main.py lifespan):

1. Fresh database: `alembic upgrade head`. Revision 0001 creates every table.
2. Existing database already built by create_all: the schema matches 0001, so
   don't re-create it. Mark it as migrated with `alembic stamp 0001`, then
   `alembic upgrade head` for anything newer.
3. Then remove `init_db()` (Base.metadata.create_all) from the API lifespan and
   worker.py, and run `alembic upgrade head` as a release step (for example, a
   one-off `docker compose run --rm api alembic upgrade head` before starting api).
   create_all never alters existing tables, so once the schema starts evolving,
   only Alembic keeps it correct.
4. Apply row-level security after migrating: `psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f sql/rls.sql`
   (Postgres only, idempotent). Re-run it whenever a migration adds an owner_id table.

Rules: never edit an applied revision; one revision per change; keep index names
SQLAlchemy-conventional (ix_<table>_<column>) so autogenerate stays quiet.
